{%- set page = nav.pages['guide'] -%}
{{ page_header(page, 'How to read the states, figures and caveats in this report.') }}
{% call panel('Explore the evidence', 'search') %}<ol><li>Start with overview denominators and records requiring review.</li><li>Search for an exact sample identifier, or select a sample in a table, chart, tree or network to open its source records.</li><li>Use global metadata filters to highlight a subset. Full-cohort summaries remain fixed and labelled; filters never change clustering or analytical results.</li><li>Select a numeric distance cell to inspect the supplied comparison and its metadata.</li><li>Inspect Methods, Limitations and Provenance before interpreting findings.</li></ol>{% endcall %}
{% call panel('Missing data and biological interpretation', 'info') %}<dl class="cf-kv"><div><dt>Present / marker detected</dt><dd>A reported detection, without a claim about expression or phenotype.</dd></div><div><dt>Absent / no marker reported</dt><dd>An assessed source call; this does not establish phenotypic susceptibility.</dd></div><div><dt>Not tested / not assessed</dt><dd>No assessment was available. Never a negative result.</dd></div><div><dt>Unavailable / invalid</dt><dd>Missing or unusable source evidence. Zero distance is a valid observation and is distinct from NA.</dd></div><div><dt>Review</dt><dd>Source records disagree or need attention. Both values are retained; no source is automatically preferred.</dd></div></dl><p>Tree topology, branch lengths and rooting are supplied by the analysis. Network geometry is a layout, not a genetic scale. Genomic clusters and network edges do not demonstrate direct transmission.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call panel('Share and archive', 'download') %}<p>Copy this HTML file alone to another computer and open it directly. Use Downloads for included records, matrices, Newick and the workflow. Use Print / Save as PDF for the complete report. Extremely large figures are better inspected in their dedicated scroll regions or exported separately.</p><p>Display options include light, dark, continuous and presentation views. Keyboard: / searches, [ and ] change sections, ? opens help, Escape closes panels. No sample records are persisted to browser storage.</p>{% endcall %}
{{ page_footer(page) }}
